{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And surely your blood.</b> Its meaning: I have permitted you to shed the blood of any living thing, except your blood — that is, of your own souls, for you are human. I have not permitted it; rather I will demand it, in the sense of \"He who demands blood,\" and this is a general principle. Afterward He clarified: \"and at the hand of man.\" If many kill an individual, or an individual kills an individual, I will demand the blood. Also I will demand it from the hand of every beast — for I will command the one [beast] that another should kill it. And so the beasts are permitted to you, but you are not permitted to them. And the one who interprets \"your blood — for your souls\" as referring to one who kills himself, is forced in my eyes. And He added to clarify: \"or He\" is a commandment to the descendants of Noah, and it is the straightforward [rule] to kill the killer."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:55.812776379Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}